# AWS EC2 deployment

This profile creates one encrypted Amazon Linux instance and runs the selected
container under Docker restart policy. It is intentionally a single-node profile.
The instance role can read only the supplied management, evaluation, and optional
database Secrets Manager ARNs; values are fetched during boot into a root-readable
environment file rather than embedded in Terraform state.

Terminate TLS at an existing load balancer or reverse proxy; the generated
instance exposes HTTP only to the explicit `allowed_cidrs`.
